%I A401787 #9 Nov 12 2026 17:01:57
%S A401787 0,0,1,0,1,2,3,2,2,1,1,5,9,8,7,7,7,6,5,4,4,3,5,6,10,13,13,15,14,14,14,
%T A401787 13,13,12,11,13,14,14,15,15,15,14,15,20,22,26,26,25,26,31,32,31,36,35,
%U A401787 38,39,44,43,43,43,44,44,43,44,45,46,46,47,46,47,46
%N A401787 a(n) is the number of prime quadruplets (q, q+2, q+6, q+8) with q strictly between p+8 and 2*(p+8), where p = A007530(n).
%C A401787 a(n) = 0 for n = 1, 2, 4 and for no other n <= 102950.
%C A401787 a(n) = 1 for n = 3, 5, 10, 11 and for no other n <= 102950.
%C A401787 Conjecture: a(n) >= 1 for all n >= 5. Verified for 5 <= n <= 102950.
%H A401787 Pankaj Ladhe, <a href="/A401787/b401787.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A401787 S. Ladhe, S. Ladhe and P. Ladhe, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22286846">An Additive Closure in the Chain of Prime Quadruplets</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%H A401787 S. Ladhe and P. Ladhe, <a href="https://github.com/SPAlgorithm/LE/tree/main/LC">lc.py: utility, checker and dataset</a>, GitHub.
%F A401787 a(n) = #{ k : A007530(n) + 8 < A007530(k) < 2*A007530(n) + 16 }.
%e A401787 For n = 3, p = 101, the largest member is 109, twice that is 218, and the only quadruplet whose first member lies strictly between 109 and 218 starts at 191, so a(3) = 1.
%Y A401787 Cf. A007530, A136162, A159910, A113404.
%K A401787 nonn,new
%O A401787 1,6
%A A401787 _Pankaj Ladhe_, Nov 05 2026
